  "summary_en": "Commission staff working document accompanying Drone Strategy 2.0. It reviews EU drone policy, the risk-based regulatory framework (open/specific/certified categories, U-space), research funding, market and sustainability benefits, consultation results, and the 2030 vision, including civil-defence synergies, standards and counter-UAS.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Reviews Regulation 2018/1139 and 2019/945 and 2019/947 establishing open, specific and certified drone categories by operational risk",
   "Describes U-space Regulations 2021/664-666 applicable from January 2023",
   "Identifies need for more European Standard Scenarios and proportionate design verification for specific-category operations",
   "Sets 2030 vision and SMART targets, including 45 cities with air mobility services and 50% European-made drone technology",
   "Promotes civil-defence dual-use synergies, common standards via EUSCG, and counter-drone resilience"
